{
  "email": "grace.okafor@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Ticket EVAL-net-04: sender cannot reach intranet from home while public internet works. Checking account status, VPN access, and sign-in block per KB-016."
}

{
  "user_id": 11,
  "reason": "KB-016/KB-013: confirm whether VPN sign-ins are reaching the server and succeeding, and whether any failures or unusual activity exist."
}

{
  "hostname": "BL-DT-0111",
  "reason": "KB-016: confirm the user's registered desktop is online and not showing warnings that could block VPN or intranet access."
}

{
  "query": "can't reach intranet from home VPN",
  "reason": "Confirm KB-016 applies to the symptom and check for any additional steps."
}

{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Grace, thanks for reporting this. Your account is active and your VPN access is turned on, and VPN sign-ins from your home network have been succeeding recently, so the account itself looks fine. Internal sites need the VPN to be connected when you're working from home. Please try these steps: 1) Connect to the VPN and wait until it shows as connected. 2) Open the intranet in a private or incognito browser window. 3) If it still doesn't load, clear your browser cache and try again. If the VPN won't connect, or it connects but the intranet still won't load, please reply to this ticket and tell us what the VPN shows (any error message) and which site or address you're trying to reach. We'll take it from there.",
  "internal_note": "Checked lookup_user: account active, vpn_access true, sign_in_blocked false, no failed logins, mailbox 35% used. Sign-in logs (last 14 days, 10 entries): all VPN and M365 sign-ins succeeded, no mfa_denied, no failed_password, no hosting-network sign-ins, all within usual hours; VPN from residential IP 198.51.100.31. Device BL-DT-0111 online, last check-in 2026-10-11, no warnings, 70% disk free. Nothing indicates an account, MFA, or security issue. Unknown: whether the user's VPN client is connected right now. The ticket does not say. Per KB-016 the escalation condition is 'VPN connected and no internal sites work', so I did not escalate yet. Asked the user to connect VPN, try a private window and clear cache, and reply with the VPN state and error. If the user confirms VPN is connected and internal sites still fail, escalate to Tier 2 with the sign-in and device results above. If VPN itself fails, follow KB-013 (Duo/client restart) before escalating.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-016",
    "KB-013"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
